<!--
    Rust match-arm labels follow the scrutinee's printed type, P9 emission;
    no option (strict bug fix, GH-883). The bytes are the native jump tables of
    kuna-native-switch-labels.xml (signed and unsigned 8/16/32/64-bit selectors,
    a signed short read through a pointer, and a sign-extended short), plus
    text8: a copy of signed8 at 0x100500 whose selector is declared char.

    The C switch printer signs its labels by the selector type, but the Rust
    match printer computed its own labels from the jump table alone. Before the
    fix every arm printed unsigned (`0xfff3 =>` on an i16, a pattern rustc
    rejects as out of range), and the sign-extended short kept the widened
    `0xfffffff3`. Both printers now share one label decision. A char spells u8
    in Rust, so text8 keeps unsigned patterns in Rust while its C switch, on a
    signed char, keeps `case -0xd:`. Lowered-switch recovery is off so these
    are native-table cases.
-->
